<main id="main" class="article-page feature-page"><header class="article-hero"><p class="eyebrow">FinOpsWay features</p><h1>Databricks All-Purpose Cluster Costs</h1><p class="article-standfirst">See cluster DBU usage and cloud infrastructure cost context beside all-purpose clusters in Databricks.</p></header><div class="article-body"><div class="feature-image-placeholder" role="img" aria-label="All-purpose cluster cost coming soon in FinOpsWay">coming soon in FinOpsWay</div><h2 id="cost-context">What makes up an all-purpose cluster cost?</h2><p>All-purpose clusters combine Databricks DBU usage with cloud virtual machine charges. The DBU rate is one part of the cost. The machines running the cluster are billed separately by the cloud provider.</p><section class="pricing-in-feature" aria-labelledby="all-purpose-rates-title"><h2 id="all-purpose-rates-title">Published all-purpose cluster rates</h2><p>Public reference rates in USD. Cloud infrastructure is a rough on-demand cost per VM hour. The final rate depends on cloud, region, node size, plan and contract.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="pricing-table" role="table"><thead role="rowgroup"><tr role="row"><th scope="col">Compute model</th><th scope="col">Cloud</th><th scope="col">Cloud infrastructure</th><th scope="col">Published compute rate</th></tr></thead><tbody role="rowgroup"><tr role="row"><td>Classic all-purpose</td><td><span class="pricing-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Cloud</span>AWS, Azure, GCP</td><td><span class="pricing-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Cloud infrastructure</span>About $0.10-$1.00+ per VM hour</td><td><span class="pricing-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Published compute rate</span>$0.55 / DBU</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note">Public reference rate checked October 6, 2026. A cluster can use several VMs. Private contract discounts are not reflected by FinOpsWay.</p><p class="pricing-region-note">Prices shown for <span class="pricing-region">US East (AWS us-east-1)</span><a href="https://www.databricks.com/product/pricing/datascience-ml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View official Databricks pricing</a>.</p></section><h2 id="workflow">How to review an all-purpose cluster</h2><ol class="feature-steps"><li><a href="/onboarding/">Connect FinOpsWay</a> and open Compute.</li><li>Read the reported cost and DBU usage beside the cluster.</li><li>Check node type, worker count and Auto Termination before changing the configuration.</li></ol><aside class="feature-advice" aria-labelledby="all-purpose-advice-title"><span class="feature-advice-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span><div><h3 id="all-purpose-advice-title">Set Auto Termination for interactive clusters</h3><p>Use a short idle timeout for shared development clusters. <a href="/guides/all-purpose-cluster-monitoring/">Read the guide to monitoring all-purpose clusters</a> before applying it to production work.</p></div></aside><h2 id="questions">Common questions</h2><h3>Does stopping a cluster remove every charge?</h3><p>It stops new DBU and cloud machine usage for that cluster. Other workspace services can still have their own charges.</p><h3>Why is the estimate different from the invoice?</h3><p>Cloud region, private terms and billing freshness can change the final amount.</p><p class="feature-limits">Billing can lag by several hours. Check the reported period and freshness.</p></div><?php include __DIR__ . '/../../includes/feature-sidebar.php'; ?></main>
